export anchor DepartureLoungeStyle:
    number: 415
    screen: TravelPlanner
    name: Departure lounge
    idea: The trip read off an airport departures board, split flap cells in monospace on black, framed by amber wayfinding signs with square pictograms and arrows, and a row of lounge seats showing who is travelling.
    base: dark
    palette:
        hall: #101114, the page, the terminal floor and the style sheet
        board: #050505, the departures board ground and fields
        flap: #1c1c1f, split flap cells, cut by a black middle line
        sign: #1f2124, wayfinding sign panels
        line: #34363b, row rules inside signs
        amber: #ffb612, sign text, pictogram squares, times, the primary button and Not booked
        onAmber: #1a1200, glyphs and text on amber
        ink: #f2efe6, flap letters and body text
        muted: #b5b0a3, sub lines and captions
        go: #5fe08a, Booked and Done
        sky: #8fd3ff, Flight rows and the focus ring
    type:
        Signs in Arial Narrow, Roboto Condensed, Helvetica Neue, Arial, bold
        caps. The board in ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas at 17px caps 600
        tracked 0.06em. The board title 34px bold caps, sign titles 20px
        bold caps in amber, column heads 13px caps tracked 0.18em, figures
        46px monospace bold.
    layout:
        A black sign bar across the top with a 4px amber rule below. On the
        left a solid amber square with a black plane and BRIGHTWORK TRIPS in
        amber caps. On the right three wayfinding links, Departures,
        Checklist and Weather, each with an outlined amber arrow box. The
        main area holds the board, black inside a 10px dark grey frame. Its
        head reads Departures over JAPAN IN APRIL with the dates in an amber
        flap cell. A table of six rows has Date, Time, Destination, Detail
        and Status, every cell a split flap tile with a black line through
        its middle. Times show in amber, missing times show dotted flaps.
        Status is a bordered box with a word. The board foot shows a row of
        six lounge seats with two filled amber for Mara Okafor plus 1 guest,
        and the buttons Book train to Kyoto and Find stay in Osaka. Below
        the board four signs sit in a row, each with a 6px amber top bar and
        an amber pictogram square. Route draws a vertical line diagram with
        Tokyo, Kyoto and Osaka as ringed stops and the train time. Checklist
        lists the four items. Budget shows 3,200 euro saved over twenty
        amber segments, thirteen lit. Weather Tokyo shows 17 degrees high
        and a pink blossom line. Below 1000px the signs go two by two and at
        phone width one per row, while the board scrolls sideways inside its
        frame.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 6px gaps between flap cells, 16px between signs and 32px above the board.
    density: Medium high. Every leg is one board row of five cells.
    corners: Square. Signs keep only a 4px lower corner.
    borders: A 10px dark grey board frame, a 6px amber bar on each sign and a 4px amber rule under the sign bar.
    shadows: None, except the 1px black split line drawn through every flap cell.
    icons:
        Black pictograms on solid amber squares and outlined amber arrows.
        Booked is a solid outlined box with a ticked square, Not booked a
        dashed box with a dashed circle, Flight a plane with no box. Done is
        a check and To do a dash.
    focus: A 3px sky blue outline offset 3px.
    tone: Terse airport caps such as Departures, Destination and Book train to Kyoto.
